1
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:32,300
"My Rival and Me"
(Episode 4)

2
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:44,740
Putting out cigarettes with your fingers?

3
00:00:45,060 --> 00:00:46,660
Think you've mastered Iron Palm kung fu?

4
00:00:50,860 --> 00:00:51,860
There.

5
00:00:52,060 --> 00:00:54,140
This medicine works best on burns.

6
00:00:54,540 --> 00:00:55,300
Doesn't hurt now, right?

7
00:00:55,380 --> 00:00:57,180
Yeah. It works well.

8
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:07,380
What medicine is this?

9
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:08,940
American cockroach extract.

10
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:15,100
Don't discriminate against species.

11
00:01:15,540 --> 00:01:18,340
I used it for burns when I worked at a
hotpot restaurant.

12
00:01:18,364 --> 00:01:19,444
Put it on, and you're good.

13
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:22,380
You worked at a hotpot restaurant too?

14
00:01:22,820 --> 00:01:23,420
Yeah.

15
00:01:23,700 --> 00:01:25,580
I've worked all sorts of jobs.

16
00:01:25,780 --> 00:01:28,900
Fruit shops, bakeries, cafes. You name it.

17
00:01:30,980 --> 00:01:32,180
What about your parents?

18
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:35,620
My mom was too busy working to look after
me.

19
00:01:35,700 --> 00:01:36,700
My dad...

20
00:01:37,060 --> 00:01:38,740
That's a whole other story.

21
00:01:43,460 --> 00:01:45,100
So that's why.

22
00:02:15,180 --> 00:02:19,020
Our veteran artist really loves his
cigarettes.

23
00:02:21,060 --> 00:02:24,380
Yet you wanted to spend 30 million on my
PR?

24
00:02:26,540 --> 00:02:27,940
You think I was lying?

25
00:02:27,980 --> 00:02:29,340
I really wanted to help.

26
00:02:29,620 --> 00:02:32,100
I've earned quite a bit from acting.

27
00:02:32,380 --> 00:02:33,740
Not 30 million yet,

28
00:02:33,980 --> 00:02:35,060
but give me some time.

29
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:49,380
Why does he look so troubled?

30
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:52,940
Even promising to study acting with him
won't help?

31
00:02:53,660 --> 00:02:59,580
Is this a veteran artist's unwavering
dedication?

32
00:03:00,580 --> 00:03:01,580
Stop smoking.

33
00:03:02,420 --> 00:03:03,940
If you really don't want to,

34
00:03:04,860 --> 00:03:05,900
then forget it.

35
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:07,420
Don't force yourself.

36
00:03:25,700 --> 00:03:26,700
I'm not.

37
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:29,180
It's settled.

38
00:03:29,580 --> 00:03:30,580
Huh?

39
00:03:44,660 --> 00:03:45,740
I'll handle it from now on.

40
00:03:57,900 --> 00:03:59,380
Thank you, Mr. Gu.

41
00:04:04,020 --> 00:04:06,420
I've never done this before,

42
00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:12,100
so I may not be very good at it.

43
00:04:13,740 --> 00:04:17,620
I don't really know the rules either.

44
00:04:18,740 --> 00:04:21,260
Anything I should watch out for?

45
00:04:21,900 --> 00:04:23,500
It's not that serious.

46
00:04:23,540 --> 00:04:25,380
Just...

47
00:04:26,020 --> 00:04:27,860
Treat you like a boyfriend?

48
00:04:30,180 --> 00:04:32,820
No need! That's going too far.

49
00:04:33,020 --> 00:04:34,740
What you're doing now is great.

50
00:04:34,940 --> 00:04:36,420
You're doing really well already.

51
00:04:38,380 --> 00:04:39,620
Just this

52
00:04:41,020 --> 00:04:43,460
counts as doing well?

53
00:04:47,140 --> 00:04:48,340
Isn't it good enough?

54
00:04:48,780 --> 00:04:52,100
A veteran artist has high standards.

55
00:04:52,180 --> 00:04:54,620
Even his fanservice has to be perfect.

56
00:04:58,020 --> 00:04:59,180
I'll work hard

57
00:05:02,020 --> 00:05:03,020
to do better.

58
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:11,500
I just need to treat you like a boyfriend.

59
00:05:12,820 --> 00:05:15,860
Why is he hung up on this boyfriend thing?

60
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:18,340
Do straight guys not know their own
strength?

61
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:21,740
I guess that works.

62
00:05:29,269 --> 00:05:30,436
[Product Letter of Intent]

63
00:05:31,860 --> 00:05:32,860
In other ways,

64
00:05:33,900 --> 00:05:36,780
there's probably not much I can do for
you.

65
00:05:37,460 --> 00:05:39,460
Here's my schedule for the second half of
the year.

66
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:41,740
Any opportunities you want?

67
00:05:41,980 --> 00:05:43,380
I'll have the company arrange them.

68
00:05:44,940 --> 00:05:45,940
Me?

69
00:05:47,620 --> 00:05:49,380
Do you have enough money?

70
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:51,260
Anything you want to buy?

71
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:52,420
I'll buy it for you.

72
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:55,180
Did you get the wrong script?

73
00:05:55,260 --> 00:05:55,940
Huh?

74
00:05:56,060 --> 00:05:57,980
This is beyond boyfriend territory.

75
00:05:58,060 --> 00:05:59,340
You're being a sugar daddy.

76
00:06:03,700 --> 00:06:05,620
If that's what you want to call me,

77
00:06:07,580 --> 00:06:08,180
that's fine.

78
00:06:08,220 --> 00:06:09,820
I'm your dad too, you know.

79
00:06:11,300 --> 00:06:14,220
Do we have to get this wild?

80
00:06:18,660 --> 00:06:21,060
I feel some mysterious force

81
00:06:21,460 --> 00:06:23,340
attacking my brain.

82
00:06:27,660 --> 00:06:28,700
Where are you going?

83
00:06:28,820 --> 00:06:29,820
To close the window.

84
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:33,540
The wind's giving you a headache.

85
00:06:42,260 --> 00:06:42,900
Oh.

86
00:06:42,940 --> 00:06:45,500
Xiao Chen told me to go to bed half an
hour ago.

87
00:06:45,580 --> 00:06:47,380
You get some sleep. I'll leave you alone.

88
00:06:49,100 --> 00:06:51,980
Shall I bring you breakfast tomorrow?

89
00:06:52,180 --> 00:06:54,060
No need. Xiao Chen will get it.

90
00:06:54,460 --> 00:06:57,580
Then I'll bring you a drink after work.

91
00:06:58,180 --> 00:07:00,020
Honey tea or milk tea?

92
00:07:00,140 --> 00:07:03,260
No need. Xiao Chen will buy it.

93
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:07,380
Then what am I for?

94
00:07:09,180 --> 00:07:11,860
Your time is precious, right?

95
00:07:12,060 --> 00:07:14,260
And I pay Xiao Chen a salary.

96
00:07:14,940 --> 00:07:16,900
Fine. I'll pay his salary.

97
00:07:19,780 --> 00:07:25,020
Then I'll pay your assistant's salary.

98
00:07:25,820 --> 00:07:27,460
How could I let you pay?

99
00:07:27,540 --> 00:07:29,180
Isn't this what I should be doing?

100
00:07:29,300 --> 00:07:32,660
He really is acting like a boyfriend.

101
00:07:32,740 --> 00:07:35,740
Is he the kind of actor who stays in
character

102
00:07:35,820 --> 00:07:38,860
and keeps our chemistry going off camera
too?

103
00:07:40,540 --> 00:07:42,020
I can't just take things from you.

104
00:07:42,140 --> 00:07:43,220
It's settled.

105
00:07:43,260 --> 00:07:45,260
Send me your assistant's payment details.

106
00:07:45,260 --> 00:07:46,980
I'll get going. Bye.

107
00:07:50,300 --> 00:07:51,300
Bye.

108
00:07:57,740 --> 00:07:59,780
Why is Gu Yiliang so strange today?

109
00:08:00,540 --> 00:08:01,580
Is he tired?

110
00:08:02,420 --> 00:08:03,460
I suppose so.

111
00:08:03,940 --> 00:08:05,900
A lot did happen today.

112
00:08:07,140 --> 00:08:08,140
Still,

113
